  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>BNEsim FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Is there a BNEsim discount code</h3>
      <p>Not one we could verify. We checked BNEsim's homepage, pricing page, and coupon page directly and found no promo code advertised. Third-party sites list codes for BNEsim that don't appear anywhere on the real site, so we're not repeating them here.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>How does BNEsim actually price its plans</h3>
      <p>Per-country and per-region data packs, each available as a cheaper 30-day-validity version or a pricier no-expiration version. Discounts of up to 70% show up as an automatic strike-through sale price rather than something you apply at checkout.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does a BNEsim plan expire</h3>
      <p>Depends which tier you buy. The standard packs expire 30 days after purchase. BNEsim also sells a pricier no-expiration version of the same packs for buyers who want the data to sit ready indefinitely.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I pay with crypto</h3>
      <p>Yes. BNEsim accepts a wider range of payment methods than most eSIM sellers on this site, crypto included, on top of standard card payment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I buy ahead of a trip and activate later</h3>
      <p>Yes. BNEsim lets you schedule a plan to start activating on a future date instead of the moment you buy it, useful if you're purchasing well ahead of departure.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

